      "id": "qvxhbg1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Matter"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Matter is defined as anything that possesses mass and occupies space.",
        "The five physical states of matter are Solid, Liquid, Gas, Plasma, and Bose-Einstein Condensate (BEC).",
        "Density is the ratio of mass to volume (Density = Mass / Volume).",
        "Elasticity is the property of a body to regain its original shape and size after removal of deforming forces.",
        "Pressure is defined as the force acting perpendicularly per unit surface area (Pressure = Force / Area)."
      ],
      "id": "cwfqz8y"
    },
